# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ask Naren service.
#
# The /ask-naren page posts to the same-origin route src/app/api/ask-naren/route.ts,
# which proxies to this URL. The only other variable under src/ is the database URL
# below (plus NODE_ENV, which Next sets itself). There are deliberately no
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars, so nothing is inlined into the client bundle.
#
# LEAVING THIS UNSET IS NOT AN ERROR, AND THAT IS THE TRAP. The default below is
# where `python ops/serve_ask_naren.py` binds, so local development needs nothing
# here at all. Anywhere else -- a container, a deployed environment -- 127.0.0.1
# is that machine itself, the route cannot connect, and it synthesises a
# `service_unreachable` decline: CSM-safe copy, HTTP 503, no crash. The page keeps
# working and simply declines everything, which reads as normal conservative
# behaviour. The signals that it is NOT are the `service_unreachable` reason code
# (never `no_close_match`), the 503 status, and a warning logged at startup.
#
# The service needs the Joveo VPN, Postgres and Pinecone -- see Brain/CLAUDE.md.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local to override. .env.local is gitignored; this one is
# the committed template and must never carry a real secret.
ASK_NAREN_SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ask Naren users and sessions (issue #44, ADR 0011).
#
# Sign-in reads and writes the `ask_naren` schema in Brain's Neon instance. This is
# the app's ONLY credential -- sessions are rows, not signed cookies, so there is
# no signing secret. A runtime variable, never NEXT_PUBLIC_*. For now it is an env
# var; the production secret store belongs to the deployment effort.
#
# UNSET, /ask-naren and /login fail with a server error that names this variable.
# Every other page works without it.
#
# ROLE ask_naren_app ONLY -- a SQL-created role granted only the ask_naren schema
# (issue #38, ADR 0012), on the POOLED host, sslmode=verify-full. Never Brain's owner
# credentials: the app checks its own role on first use and REFUSES to serve one that
# could reach Brain's tables. Setup: db/provision/README.md.
ASK_NAREN_DATABASE_URL=

# The users CLI (`npm run users -- --help`) connects as ask_naren_admin, the only role
# that can create users and set passwords -- deliberately not the web app's.
ASK_NAREN_ADMIN_DATABASE_URL=

# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY, ignored in production: skip the least-privilege check for a
# local database whose only role is a superuser (PGlite's socket server, a laptop
# Postgres). Never set this against Neon.
# ASK_NAREN_SKIP_PRIVILEGE_CHECK=1
